00:05:21.518 --> 00:05:26.278
Arceumons, in observations shared on the space subreddit, shows gas emissions close

00:05:26.278 --> 00:05:30.738
to the volcano that could indicate conditions beneath the surface more hospitable to life

00:05:30.738 --> 00:05:31.918
than previously thought.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:36.718
The finding comes from data collected near one of the solar system's largest volcanoes,

00:05:37.318 --> 00:05:41.538
and researchers noted the presence of the gas and proximity to the volcano's flanks.

00:05:41.978 --> 00:05:47.018
This location has drawn attention because volcanic heat could maintain liquid water or other

00:05:47.018 --> 00:05:48.138
volatiles at depth.

00:05:48.138 --> 00:05:54.098
The emissions suggest chemical processes that might support microbial activity if they reach the surface.

00:05:54.658 --> 00:06:00.298
Further analysis of orbital spectra helped isolate the gas signature from background atmospheric readings.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:04.400
Nuclear propulsion systems, interesting engineering reports,

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:08.620
offer higher efficiency than chemical rockets for long duration missions

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:13.140
and could shorten travel times to Mars and beyond while carrying heavier payloads.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:17.880
Nuclear thermal designs heat propellant to higher temperatures than chemical combustion

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:23.140
allows, and that produces greater exhaust velocity and reduces the mass of propellant needed.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:27.920
Engineers note that the technology builds on decades of reactor research originally

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.680
developed for terrestrial power.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:34.660
Integration with existing launch vehicles would require new shielding and safety protocols.

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:39.920
The higher specific impulse opens routes to outer planets that chemical stages cannot reach

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.580
within reasonable crew timelines.

00:06:42.711 --> 00:06:47.091
David Gill captured the first successful wide-field photograph of a comet from the Cape

00:06:47.091 --> 00:06:53.571
of Good Hope Observatory on November 7, 1882, Astronomy Reports, and the image demonstrated

00:06:53.571 --> 00:06:57.251
that long exposures could record faint detail invisible to the eye.

00:06:57.791 --> 00:07:02.711
The comet had reached naked eye visibility during daylight at Parahelion two months earlier.

00:07:03.371 --> 00:07:08.551
Gill used a portrait lens mounted on an equatorial telescope to track the object across several

00:07:08.551 --> 00:07:08.951
hours.

00:07:08.951 --> 00:07:14.531
The resulting plate showed the comet's tail structure and surrounding starfield in a single frame.

00:07:15.011 --> 00:07:20.751
This success encouraged other observatories to adopt photographic methods for systematic sky surveys.

00:07:21.801 --> 00:07:30.651
Supernova 2026 avu appears in the Bard Safered Galaxy NGC 14,333, according to the space subreddit.

00:07:31.321 --> 00:07:37.521
A Type 1A event discovered November 2nd by the Atlas Survey in a Galaxy 46 million light years away

00:07:37.521 --> 00:07:40.981
that shows active star formation along its spiral arms.

00:07:41.561 --> 00:07:46.981
Type 1A events occur when a white dwarf reaches the Chandrasekhar limit and detonates, giving

00:07:46.981 --> 00:07:52.121
astronomers a standard candle whose peak brightness is consistent enough to measure cosmic distances,

00:07:52.761 --> 00:07:57.261
and the same process seeds the universe with iron peak elements, including much of the

00:07:57.261 --> 00:07:58.961
iron now found in human blood.

00:07:59.561 --> 00:08:05.661
NGC 1433 features a double ringed central structure formed by tightly wound spiral arms along its

00:08:05.661 --> 00:08:12.201
bar. Atlas uses 4.5 meter telescopes to image the entire sky multiple times each night.

00:08:12.841 --> 00:08:18.361
Once confirmed as a Type-1A event, the supernovas light curve can refine the distance to NGC

00:08:19.801 --> 00:08:25.901
14133 without relying solely on other indicators. The explosion leaves no compact remnant because

00:08:25.901 --> 00:08:31.754
the runaway fusion consumes the entire star. On the same round of notes, families explored

